<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>

    <!-- NuGet Package Metadata -->
    <PackageId>Sendspin.SDK</PackageId>
    <Version>9.3.2</Version>
    <Authors>Sendspin Contributors</Authors>
    <Company>Sendspin</Company>
    <Product>Sendspin SDK</Product>
    <Description>Cross-platform SDK for the Sendspin synchronized multi-room audio protocol. Connect to Music Assistant servers and play synchronized audio across multiple devices.</Description>
    <PackageTags>sendspin;audio;multiroom;sync;music-assistant;streaming</PackageTags>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v9.3.2 - Discovery (9.x legacy line):

One fix: players are now reliably discoverable by servers. No API changes.

- The mDNS advertiser announces its presence instead of only answering
  queries. Advertising registered the records with a passive query responder
  and multicast nothing, while a server's mDNS browser stops broadcasting
  the service type once its startup queries are done - so a player that
  started after the server was never discovered at all, and discovery only
  appeared to work when the player was already running when the server came
  up. The advertiser now multicasts its records unsolicited (RFC 6762
  section 8.3) when advertising starts, and again whenever a network
  interface appears - resume from sleep, a late-associating Wi-Fi - since
  the announcement sent before that interface existed never reached it. The
  announcement carries the full PTR/SRV/TXT/A set, so a server can connect
  from its cache alone.

Note: staying visible past the records' TTL still requires the player to
hear the server's refresh queries, so allow inbound UDP 5353 through any
host firewall.

----

      Earlier release notes: https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet/releases
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2024-2026 Sendspin Contributors</Copyright>

    <!-- Enable source link for debugging -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

    <!-- Generate XML documentation -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- NativeAOT and trimming compatibility -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Sendspin.SDK.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Core dependencies - all cross-platform -->
    <PackageReference Include="Concentus" Version="2.2.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Zeroconf" Version="3.7.16" />
    <PackageReference Include="Makaretu.Dns.Multicast" Version="0.27.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="8.0.5" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="8.0.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
